---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import ConceptImage from '../../components/ConceptImage.astro';
import CTA from '../../components/CTA.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Whole-Home Renovations in North Alabama"
  description="Plan a whole-home renovation in North Alabama around room flow, practical phasing, and your budget. Share your property and priorities with Apex."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Renovations / Whole-home"
    title="One home. A more considered whole."
    description="A whole-home renovation is more than a collection of room updates. It is a chance to think about how your home connects, how you live in it, and what should come next."
    image="/assets/living-concept.webp"
    alt="AI-generated whole-home renovation concept with an open living area and warm natural finishes"
  >
    <a class="button button-gold" href="/start-your-project/">Start your project <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="home-scope">
    <div class="wrap split-content">
      <div class="prose">
        <span class="eyebrow">Look at the bigger picture</span>
        <h2 id="home-scope">Keep what works.<br />Rethink what doesn’t.</h2>
        <p>For homeowners in North Alabama, whole-home renovation starts with understanding the existing property. Which spaces feel disconnected? Where is storage missing? Which finishes still serve you well? Your answers help distinguish essential changes from nice-to-have updates.</p>
        <p>Your brief might include flooring across connected rooms, interior finishes, storage, kitchen and bathroom updates, or ideas for a different room arrangement. Describe the outcome first. Any layout or building-system changes need assessment before becoming part of an agreed scope.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/renovations/kitchens-bathrooms/">Focus on kitchens &amp; bathrooms <span aria-hidden="true"><Icon name="arrow-up-right" /></span></a>
      </div>
      <ConceptImage src="/assets/kitchen-concept.webp" alt="AI-generated concept of a kitchen opening into a connected living space" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-stone" aria-labelledby="home-planning">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Plan around real life</span>
        <h2 id="home-planning">The right sequence matters.</h2>
        <p>A considered plan connects the desired finish with the practical realities of getting there.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="feature-card">
          <span class="number">01</span>
          <h3>Flow between spaces</h3>
          <p>Consider sightlines, transitions, and daily routes through the home. A consistent material palette can connect rooms without making every space identical.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <span class="number">02</span>
          <h3>Phasing &amp; occupancy</h3>
          <p>Let us know whether you plan to stay in the home. Access, work areas, and essential rooms all affect whether a phased approach is practical.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="feature-card">
          <span class="number">03</span>
          <h3>Budget boundaries</h3>
          <p>Separate must-haves from later improvements. Discuss allowances for unknown conditions, and identify which decisions need your approval before scope changes move forward.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="home-faq">
    <div class="wrap split-content">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Whole-home questions</span>
        <h2 id="home-faq">Room for a clearer plan.</h2>
        <p>Renovating a rental instead? Explore a different set of priorities for <a class="text-link" href="/renovations/investment-properties/">investment properties</a>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details>
          <summary>Do all rooms need to be renovated at once?</summary>
          <p>Not necessarily. A phased plan may make sense, but shared finishes, access, and work that affects adjoining rooms should be considered together. Discuss the full wish list early so a first phase does not overlook later plans.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can I remain in the home during the renovation?</summary>
          <p>That depends on the work, site conditions, and access to essential spaces. Do not assume every scope is compatible with occupancy. Raise household needs during assessment so disruption and any alternative arrangements can be discussed.</p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What determines the price and schedule?</summary>
          <p>The size and condition of the home, selected materials, extent of changes, and sequencing all matter. Pricing requires assessment. Timing also depends on decisions, availability, and any required approvals, so a fixed completion period would be premature.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA title="A home that feels more like yours." text="Tell us what you want to keep, what you want to change, and what matters most. Start with the bigger picture." />
</SiteLayout>
